---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CallCTA from '../components/CallCTA.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site.js';

const title = 'Hand-Raised Sugar Gliders for Sale Philippines';
const description =
  'Bonded, hand-raised sugar glider joeys from ₱13,000 with DENR papers included and in-person delivery. Temperament-matched and supported for life. Call to reserve.';

// Home carries Organization, WebSite and FAQPage.
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How much is a sugar glider in the Philippines?',
    a: 'Our hand-raised joeys start at ₱13,000, with the full DENR paperwork included in that price. A rarer colour or a bonded pair costs more. Call us for the exact figure for the joey you want.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are sugar gliders legal to keep in the Philippines?',
    a: 'Yes, with proper documentation. They sit under wildlife regulation as a non-native species, so legal ownership should be registered. Every joey we place comes with full DENR paperwork, with ownership recorded in your name.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long do sugar gliders live?',
    a: 'Ten to fifteen years with good care, which makes them a long-term commitment rather than a short-term pet.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  schema={['FAQPage']}
  faqs={faqs}
  ogType="website"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="hero__eyebrow">Hand-raised. Documented. Bonded before they are yours.</p>
      <h1>Hand-Raised Sugar Gliders for Sale in the Philippines</h1>
      <p class="hero__lede">
        A palm-sized marsupial that learns the sound of your voice, sleeps against
        your heartbeat, and stays close for more than a decade. Ours are raised by
        hand from the moment they leave the pouch, so the bond begins long before
        you meet. If you have been looking for sugar gliders for sale in the
        Philippines and want one that is already used to people, this is where the
        search ends.
      </p>
      <CallCTA bare />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="mt-0">The difference you can feel in five minutes</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        There is a wide gap between a joey hand-raised in a home and an animal
        pulled from a glass tank at a weekend stall. One has been held every day
        since its eyes opened. The other has learned that hands mean stress.
      </p>
      <p class="muted" style="max-width:44rem;">
        Every glider here is raised the first way. We know each one by temperament
        before it ever goes home, which is the part that decides whether your first
        month is a friendship or a fight.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="mt-0">What you bring home</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>A genuinely bonded joey</h3>
          <p>Handled daily from out-of-pouch, so it already trusts the weight and warmth of a person.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>A temperament match, not a transaction</h3>
          <p>We pair you with the joey that suits your household, your patience, and your handling experience. A first-time keeper and a seasoned one do not get the same animal.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Full DENR paperwork, every purchase</h3>
          <p>Legal ownership documented in your name. No grey areas, no animal you have to hide.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Support that outlasts the handover</h3>
          <p>The first weeks decide everything. You can reach us through them, and after.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="mt-0">What life with one is actually like</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        They wake at dusk. They will ride in a bonding pouch against your chest
        while you cook, glide the length of a room to land on your shoulder, and
        make a soft purring chatter that owners spend years trying to describe.
        Kept well, they live ten to fifteen years, which means the joey you reserve
        now is a companion for the next decade of your life.
      </p>
      <p class="muted" style="max-width:44rem;">
        That length is the whole point. It is also the reason we are slow about who
        we place them with.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:46rem;">
      <h2 class="mt-0">An honest word before you decide</h2>
      <p>
        Sugar gliders are not a starter pet, and we would rather tell you that now
        than after.
      </p>
      <p>
        They are nocturnal, so your evenings become their mornings. They are social
        to the point that a lone glider can decline, which is why we place them in
        bonded pairs unless your home already has one waiting. They need a tall
        enclosure, a real diet, and a keeper who reads up before the joey arrives,
        not after.
      </p>
      <p>
        If that sounds like a commitment rather than an impulse, you are exactly the
        kind of home we look for. Start with the <a href="/care-guide">Care Guide</a>
        if you are still deciding. There is no rush, and we will still be here.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:46rem;">
      <h2 class="mt-0">When you are ready, so is your joey</h2>
      <p>
        Call us and we will tell you which of the gliders here would thrive in your
        home, what the paperwork covers, the exact price for the pairing you want,
        and how we deliver to your area in person.
      </p>
      <CallCTA />
      <p class="center muted" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        Or <a href="/available-joeys">see the joeys available now →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
